# Database & API Strategy for ACONCCI Notes App

## Goal Description
Transition from basic `AsyncStorage` to a robust database (SQLite) and define API requirements for cloud features. This will improve performance, data integrity, and enable future sync/sharing features.

## Proposed Changes

### [Database] SQLite Schema
A relational database like `expo-sqlite` is recommended for local persistence.

#### `notes` table
- [id](file:///c:/Users/USER/ACONCCInotesapp/types/note.ts#68-74): TEXT (Primary Key)
- `title`: TEXT
- `content`: TEXT
- `type`: TEXT (vault, sticky, journal, plain_text, voice, image, video, drawing, checklist, reminder)
- `createdAt`: TEXT (ISO 8601)
- `updatedAt`: TEXT (ISO 8601)
- `categoryId`: TEXT (Foreign Key -> categories.id)
- `isFavorite`: INTEGER (0/1)
- `isPinned`: INTEGER (0/1)
- `isArchived`: INTEGER (0/1)
- `isTrashed`: INTEGER (0/1)
- `color`: TEXT
- `isMarkdown`: INTEGER (0/1)
- `lastOpenedAt`: TEXT (ISO 8601)
- `metadata`: TEXT (JSON string for type-specific fields like `moodEmoji`, `audioUrl`, `checklistItems`)

#### `categories` table
- [id](file:///c:/Users/USER/ACONCCInotesapp/types/note.ts#68-74): TEXT (Primary Key)
- `name`: TEXT
- `color`: TEXT
- `icon`: TEXT
- `parentId`: TEXT (Self-referential FK)
- `createdAt`: TEXT (ISO 8601)

#### `tags` table
- [id](file:///c:/Users/USER/ACONCCInotesapp/types/note.ts#68-74): TEXT (Primary Key)
- `name`: TEXT
- `color`: TEXT
- `createdAt`: TEXT (ISO 8601)

#### `note_tags` (Join table)
- `noteId`: TEXT (FK -> notes.id)
- `tagId`: TEXT (FK -> tags.id)

### [API] Requirements & Strategy
For features requiring a backend, we recommend a "Backend-as-a-Service" like **Supabase** or **Firebase**.

#### Sync API
- `POST /sync`: Push local changes and pull remote updates.
- `GET /notes`: Retrieve all notes for a user (with pagination).

#### Media API
- `POST /upload`: Upload audio/image/video files to cloud storage (S3/Supabase Storage).
- `GET /media/:id`: Retrieve signed URLs for media.

#### AI API (Optional)
- `POST /transcribe`: Convert voice notes to text.
- `POST /summarize`: Generate summaries for long notes.

